# Learn more https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files

# dependencies
node_modules/
_package-lock.json

# package-lock.json is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It was, and that meant nothing pinned the dependency tree: this machine
# installs with npm, Replit installs fresh, and the two were free to resolve
# different versions of the same caret range. Every dependency in package.json
# that starts with ^ or ~ is a version this app has never been tested against
# waiting to be installed. That kind of drift surfaces as a bug that reproduces
# on one machine and not the other, which is the most expensive kind to chase —
# and this project has already lost days to failures that could not be
# reproduced locally.

# Expo
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts

# Native
ios/
android/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# Metro
.metro-health-check*

# debug
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.pem

# local env files
.env*.local

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
.vercel

.env

# Claude Code — machine-local only. launch.json IS committed: the preview/dev-server
# tooling needs it, and it describes the project, not the machine.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/*.lock
